From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Wed, 2 Sep 2026 11:52:31 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 3/4] Automated status decisions, per-role technical tests with
 auto-grading, two-way ClickUp sync
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

- Score policy (AUTO_STATUS_ENABLED, REJECT_BELOW=50, SELECT_ABOVE=60): <50 rejected,
  50-60 filtered, >60 selected — or test_sent when the role defines a written test.
  Only fires on status 'new'; never overrides human/ClickUp decisions.
- Role form: test questions + private answer key. Qualifying candidates receive a unique
  one-submission online test link by email (Gmail SMTP via MAIL_USERNAME/MAIL_PASSWORD;
  falls back to posting the link on the ClickUp task when mail is unconfigured).
- Candidate test page /test/<token>; on submit Claude grades against the answer key,
  status -> test_returned, full result comment posted on ClickUp tagging the team.
- ClickUp -> app webhook /webhooks/clickup (taskStatusUpdated, HMAC-verified) +
  'flask clickup-webhook-setup' registration command; loop-safe echo handling.
- Additive auto-migration adds new columns to existing tables on startup.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01JcN7fd3GzJkJXg5WQpuUjU
