From 7a4ac0c5025ba9bdea4d91248720b77313f215da Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Thu, 3 Sep 2026 10:46:07 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 4/4] Fix test-email delivery and make ClickUp two-way sync
 fully automatic
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

User testing found: (1) test emails were not reaching candidates, (2) board-side status
changes were not reflected in the app.

- Mail: new gmail_api backend that reuses the GOOGLE_OAUTH_* (Drive) credentials — no Gmail
  App Password needed; gdrive_auth.py now also requests gmail.send. Backend auto-selected:
  smtp if MAIL_USERNAME/PASSWORD set, else gmail_api if Google creds present, else off.
- Never claim TEST SENT unless the mail actually left; process-pending retries unsent tests
  and promotes to test_sent on success; admin per-applicant Send/Resend-test button.
- Dashboard system banner: live email status + 'Send test email' diagnostic, ClickUp sync
  mode (WEBHOOK ACTIVE / POLLING ONLY).
- ClickUp -> app sync needs zero setup now: webhook self-registers at startup (secret kept
  in a new settings table, used for HMAC verification), plus a polling reconciler every
  CLICKUP_POLL_MINUTES (default 10) that adopts board changes and re-pushes recent app
  changes that never landed — statuses converge even without the webhook.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01JcN7fd3GzJkJXg5WQpuUjU
